nd a high child (true), down to the constants (Bryant,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“Graph-Based Algorithms for Boolean Function Manipulation”, 1986).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Variables are tested in index order, 0 nearest the root. The table never holds two vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that test the same variable with the same children, nor a vertex whose children are equal, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each function has one vertex: two "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values are equal exactly when they are the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)          \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)              \/\/ 5","diagram.vertexCount(of: f)                            \/\/ 5: x0, x1, x2 and both constants","let g = diagram.restrict(f, variable: 2, to: false)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1","g == diagram.and(x0, x1)                              \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functions are built by the mutating methods, which add vertices to the table and leave every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text